WEBVTT

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.320
Hey, have you heard?

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:02.010
A guy in second year got in an 
accident around here recently.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.230
He was on his bike going to pick up his girlfriend

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.610
and he crashed into a street phone pole.

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:10.400
Jeez.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:11.860
And he died?

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:19.570
<i>Could that guy be the one that died?</i>

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:26.700
<i>What?</i>

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:34.590
<i>A bat person?</i>

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.970
Hey, you can't stay like that forever.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:40.760
Oh, really?

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.970
You'll take the curse, right? 
You will, right?

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:47.730
Ah, sure.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:52.100
You will, right? Then we have a deal.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.380
<i>Curse?</i>

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:00.200
Curs

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.050
<i>I'm pretty sure...</i>

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:03.930
Curse

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.820
<i>he wrote it wrong.</i>

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:12.110
What are you looking at, Sakura-chan?

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:13.040
Nothing.

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:16.070
<i>Weird.</i>

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:19.360
<i>I've never seen anything like it.</i>

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:23.720
Curse of the Rabbit Hutch

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.350
Morning, Rokudou-kun.

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:27.950
Mamiya Sakura.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:30.470
A request letter?

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:32.420
I think so.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:36.730
"Help me, I've been cursed."

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:41.460
"My boyfriend was in a bike 
accident three days ago."

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:44.740
"I'll tell you more on the rooftop."

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.870
Could this be...

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:50.930
Yeah, this is ominous.

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:53.010
Rokudou-kun.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:55.500
They didn't leave any money or offerings.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.440
Oh, that?

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:04.930
<i>Some of the characters are wrong.</i>

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:06.310
<i>Huh?</i>

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.530
<i>This handwriting...</i>

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:17.540
So those two are the stingy clients.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:21.490
Were you the ones that sent this letter?

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:22.550
Huh?

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:24.910
It said you wanted me to come up 
because you have to talk.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:26.080
What?

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:28.170
This is ominous.

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:30.580
I hope I don't have a business competitor.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:33.490
Some of the characters are wrong.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:38.210
Rokudou-kun, it's the same 
handwriting as the request letter.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:40.590
I wonder if someone's playing a prank.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:42.970
You're right.

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.110
But why?

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:47.790
It's true that my boyfriend 
was in an accident.

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:48.440
Huh?

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:56.230
Fall!

00:04:56.990 --> 00:04:59.860
<i>That writing... it's the 
spirit from the phone pole.</i>

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:01.230
What is it, Minami?

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:02.070
Damn.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:10.280
I'll get you for this!

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.010
Are you all right, Minami?

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:15.250
It felt like something grabbed my neck.

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:17.620
There's finger marks on your neck!

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:19.810
I shook it off frantically.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:20.630
I'm scared.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:23.380
It could have been bad if you 
weren't in the wrestling club.

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:26.630
Wrestling club, huh? Wow.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.710
<i>Minami Suzu, class 2-2.</i>

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.370
<i>And her classmate, Tadano Tomoya.</i>

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:37.980
<i>The spirit from earlier was 
her boyfriend, Todoroki Reiji.</i>

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:37.980
Spirit: Todoroki Reiji
 Friends                 Dating
Classmates

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:40.810
Reiji's become a wandering spirit?

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:43.760
That's crazy.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:44.990
It can't be true.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:47.090
But it's true.

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.970
That's not what I mean.

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:51.870
Reiji's still...

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:54.620
He's still alive, isn't he?

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:58.210
He's alive? But he's a spirit.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:04.460
Three days ago, Reiji got in a bike 
accident on his way to pick me up.

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:10.920
He ran out of gas, and there just happened 
to be a phone pole when he stumbled.

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:14.410
Reiji.

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:18.360
<i>Would you call that a bike accident?</i>

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:20.600
Moyori General Hospital

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:28.990
Maybe he got hit in a bad spot; 
he hasn't woken up since.

00:06:29.310 --> 00:06:30.870
Of course he wouldn't.

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:33.660
We need to bring his living 
spirit back to his body.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:34.990
His living spirit?

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:38.670
It's when your soul leaves your 
body while you're still alive.

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:41.880
The body here is an empty husk.

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:46.870
To wake him up, we have to find the living 
spirit and bring it back to his body.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:52.350
Rokudou-kun, I've seen Reiji-san's 
living spirit before.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:53.440
Really?

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:54.440
Is that true?

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:58.770
And some person that looked 
like a bat took him away.

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:00.230
A bat?

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:05.880
What the?

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:07.320
It sounds like a bike.

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:09.270
<i>That's odd.</i>

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:11.540
<i>The spirit is creating poltergeist noise.</i>

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:14.580
<i>These two can hear it?</i>

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:20.190
Reiji?

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:21.000
Why?

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:23.500
These two can see the spirit, too?

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:26.310
Suzu. Tomoya.

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:30.720
You've been seeing each other since 
I've been in the hospital, haven't you?

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:31.770
What?

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:33.250
Is that true?

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:34.510
No, no.

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:36.400
You're not fooling me!

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:38.310
I'll curse you!

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:43.330
Get back!

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:51.400
<i>A cash card?</i>

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:01.910
You're that guy.

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:06.170
Is this your doing?

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:07.250
Quite heinous.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:11.550
If that's how you feel, why 
don't you stop me, Rinne-kun?

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:13.470
You know him?

00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:19.340
I haven't for one day forgotten my 
hatred for you, Rinne-kun.

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:21.340
Your spite is misplaced.

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:23.890
All I did was exorcise a demon.

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:25.270
Demon?

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:29.250
Exactly. I'm a demon.

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:34.660
And for all this time, Rokudou Rinne, 
I hated you and awaited my revenge.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:36.110
Revenge?

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:38.030
But why?

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:39.850
I'll tell you.

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:42.330
It was six years ago.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:45.920
I was in fourth year demon school elementary.

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:50.300
Everyone, it's summer 
break starting tomorrow.

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:52.250
Your homework for the summer

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:57.250
is to take an unsalvaged soul 
in the living world to Hell.

00:08:57.250 --> 00:08:58.800
Okay.

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:06.810
I chose the soul of a rabbit 
dying of loneliness.

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:09.760
Poor you.

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:14.100
I bet everyone's forgotten about 
you and gone off having fun.

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:19.040
There's no point in living.

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:21.240
Now, let's bring you peace.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:25.260
I was just about to take the rabbit's soul.

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:26.460
But just then...

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:28.540
It's not dead yet.

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:29.700
Who are you?!

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:32.100
Class 4-2, Rokudou Rinne.

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:33.660
I'm in charge of the animals.

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:36.340
Huh? You seem kind of wealthy.

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:38.430
My grandpa was still alive at the time.

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:42.900
I'd buy popsicles nearly every day.

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:45.520
I don't care to hear your reminiscing.

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:52.250
Don't worry, Usako-chan, 
we haven't forgotten about you.

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:55.570
Here.

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:04.160
You bastard, it was almost dead!

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:07.660
Take this, Devil Fork!

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:09.460
You're a demon?

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:11.000
Then...

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:13.840
Fool! That wouldn't stop me!

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.340
Ow, ow!

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:22.350
So... that's why you hate him?

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:24.490
I was a kid, too.

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:26.070
I didn't know when to stop.

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:30.770
The night watch teacher caught me, 
and I got in deep trouble for fighting.

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:33.840
I was so worried they'd 
call our guardians.

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:35.370
That's not all.

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:38.990
Chick Catching

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:39.810
The colored chick that was 
left unsold at the festival.

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:49.640
The goldfish in the tank that'd been left 
unmaintained until it was green with algae.

00:10:54.610 --> 00:10:56.640
Even the brown cicada that was

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:58.750
nearing the end of its life 
two weeks after it'd emerged.

00:11:01.190 --> 00:11:04.390
You got in my way at every turn.

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:07.410
I couldn't do my homework because of you,

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:09.700
and I got put on detention on the 
first day of the second term.

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:14.900
That day, I made a promise to the 
weight of the buckets in my hands.

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:18.740
Rinne-kun, I will 
have my revenge on you.

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:19.990
That's awful.

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:22.530
You got Reiji caught up in all 
this for something <i>that</i> petty?

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:26.240
My name is Masato.

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:29.830
Written "evil," "narrow," "person."

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:28.120
Evil

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:28.870
Evil

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:31.870
Evil

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:31.870
Masato.

00:11:32.310 --> 00:11:34.790
No one is as narrow-minded as I am.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:39.800
Evil

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:39.800
You wrote it wrong.

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:42.300
You can't even write your own name?

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:43.650
Shut up!

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:46.770
I'm taking him in place of that rabbit.

00:11:46.770 --> 00:11:48.810
Eventually I'll bring him to Hell.

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:50.150
No!

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:52.350
Reiji isn't the same as a rabbit!

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:55.290
There's six years worth of interest

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:57.440
on the souls of the chick, 
the goldfish and the cicada.

00:11:57.680 --> 00:11:59.440
That's so petty.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:01.300
I'm Masato.

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:04.450
No one is as petty as I am.

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:06.280
You're not getting away!

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:10.580
He disappeared.

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:12.840
<i>He escaped into the Reidou.</i>

00:12:16.530 --> 00:12:18.750
Take this, Devil Fire!

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:24.770
Shoot, I can't fight if my Haori 
of the Underworld burns up.

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:30.370
Damn, I lost him.

00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:40.280
Moyori General Hospital

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:42.850
So Reiji's still alive.

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:45.820
Yet he's taking his living spirit to Hell.

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:48.550
The longer the spirit 
stays away from the body,

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:51.670
the harder it becomes for it to return.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:54.210
What? Then we have to hurry.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:55.830
We can't waste a minute.

00:12:56.270 --> 00:13:00.970
But Masato is telling Reiji's 
soul all kinds of lies

00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:02.880
to turn him into a living, evil spirit.

00:13:03.270 --> 00:13:05.550
That's why Reiji was saying such things.

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:08.890
You've been seeing each other since 
I've been in the hospital, haven't you?

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:11.100
What do we do?

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:13.690
He has to want to return.

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:16.350
It's not like he's a runaway child.

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:18.900
Don't you have any happy 
memories together or anything?

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:20.650
Memories?

00:13:20.970 --> 00:13:25.160
Talk to him about happy memories of 
when you first met. Have him remember.

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:29.160
That way he might want to come back.

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:30.870
That's a good idea.

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:33.740
Happy memories?

00:13:35.270 --> 00:13:39.250
Let's see, it was back when 
we first started dating.

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:44.910
Things were starting to get kind of 
good at the end of our first date.

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:47.610
Suzu, I love you!

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:54.100
I got excited and put a 
suplex on him by accident.

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:56.100
Greco-Roman style.

00:13:56.710 --> 00:13:58.950
I pulled it off perfectly.

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:01.170
I would have gotten
5 points at a competition.

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:03.850
<i>That's your happy memory?</i>

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:05.440
I have more.

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:09.880
He bought me a crepe when we were on a date.

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:12.590
I dropped cream on my skirt.

00:14:13.380 --> 00:14:15.280
Let's wipe it off before it becomes a stain.

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:20.880
I put a tawara throw on him 
by accident out of habit.

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:23.310
You were on asphalt, weren't you?

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:25.950
Reiji-san didn't do anything wrong.

00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:27.130
And then...

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:30.950
When I was just about to 
give him a love letter...

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:37.390
I got so embarrassed, I put an 
Argentine backbreaker on him.

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:40.310
I give, I give!

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:44.040
That's the wrong kind of happy.

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:47.230
And that's not even wrestling; 
that's pro wrestling.

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:50.410
I'm surprised Reiji-san 
still went out with you.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:51.920
You have to take care of him.

00:14:52.350 --> 00:14:54.650
We were so happy.

00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:59.270
You were, huh?

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:04.340
You're going to work for free, Rinne-sama?!

00:15:04.660 --> 00:15:06.280
I don't have a choice.

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:11.850
Reiji-san's a casualty of Rokudou-kun 
and Masato-kun's problems.

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:13.220
No way.

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:17.470
Oh yeah, I found this.

00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:22.560
It's a Demon Bank cash card!

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:26.580
Masato-kun left it in the 
hospital room after he threw it.

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:28.780
How careless of him.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:32.320
Let's say we withdraw all his 
savings and make him despair.

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:34.780
We don't know his PIN, though.

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:37.910
That doof has it written right on here!

00:15:38.380 --> 00:15:40.580
Is he stupid? Or is it a trap?

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:43.550
Half-and-half.

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.420
Please do not allow others to use this card.
 Please hold onto this card with care.
 If this card is ever lost or stolen, please report to Demon Bank main office.
 Please beware that bending, freezing, burning, electrocuting or otherwise damaging this card may render it unusable.
 PIN: 4-4-4-4
 Demon Bank

00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:48.130
That's an easy number to memorize.

00:15:48.490 --> 00:15:50.760
So why did he write it down?

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:52.940
Maybe it's because he can't remember.

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:55.140
Is he stupid? Is it a trap?

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:56.900
Seventy-thirty.

00:15:56.900 --> 00:15:58.260
Maybe eighty-twenty?

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:01.870
So either way, he's stupid.

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:06.430
Mamiya-san.

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:09.110
What's up, Suzu-senpai?

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:11.780
Reiji's started putting curses in people.

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:12.360
Huh?

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:16.870
 Cursed

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:16.870
Idiot
 Reiji was here

00:16:13.190 --> 00:16:14.090
Look.

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:16.110
See what he did to my lunch.

00:16:16.110 --> 00:16:16.870
Wow.

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:18.850
It's weak, but I hate it.

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:21.380
It kind of makes you lose 
your appetite, doesn't it?

00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:24.250
And there's scribbles on my textbook.

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:27.280
A flipbook comic?

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:30.260
I think he got bored of 
drawing it part way through.

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:33.200
That's kind of sad, isn't it?

00:16:34.030 --> 00:16:35.300
Where's Tomoya-senpai?

00:16:37.190 --> 00:16:38.600
That's Tomoya's voice.

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:41.770
He just collapsed.

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:44.270
Why are there tire marks on him?

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:46.400
Tomoya!

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:47.520
That's awful.

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:53.650
He's awful.

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:57.490
<i>Suzu-senpai can't see him.</i>

00:16:57.490 --> 00:17:01.490
I don't know what the demon told 
him, but he's got to be stupid.

00:17:02.150 --> 00:17:03.000
Um...

00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:05.090
I hate him!

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:06.750
I'm not going to visit him anymore!

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:11.880
Tomoya, hang in there.

00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:14.760
<i>Reiji-san.</i>

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:18.940
Human bonds are fragile.

00:17:18.940 --> 00:17:22.750
Reiji's living spirit will go to Hell, 
never to return to his body.

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:27.060
And I've set up one more terrible trap.

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:31.400
When Rinne-kun finally succumbs to 
his poverty and uses the cash card...

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:37.320
Sucker! Sucker! Sucker!

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:37.320
<i>His terrible trap: the end.</i>

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:39.820
Sheesh, lame.

00:17:40.170 --> 00:17:41.790
Rokudou-kun.

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:46.480
He's not here.

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:49.430
I'm in a hurry.

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:52.000
Sakura-sama.

00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:55.010
Rokumon-chan, perfect.

00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:58.380
Suzu, you idiot!

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:01.840
Reiji-san!

00:18:01.840 --> 00:18:05.430
Let's go apologize to 
Suzu-senpai and Tomoya-senpai.

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:07.230
I'll go apologize with you.

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:08.390
No!

00:18:08.390 --> 00:18:10.560
They're the ones that betrayed me!

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:12.650
They started dating behind my back!

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:15.150
Masato-kun lied to you.

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:18.690
You won't be able to go back to 
your body if you keep this up.

00:18:18.690 --> 00:18:20.160
You'll really end up dead!

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:25.790
Th-Th-Th-This is...

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:30.920
S-Suzu and Tomoya kissing!

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:36.380
That's a shame, Reiji.

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:38.590
There's no place for you left in this world.

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:41.090
No way, that's not going to work.

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:46.350
The sign in the back is inverted, 
and they're not the right height.

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:48.430
It's obviously 'shopped.

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:52.700
On what planet would there be 
anyone that could fall for this?

00:18:52.700 --> 00:18:55.080
It's over.

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:56.190
What?

00:18:56.670 --> 00:18:58.670
It's no use, Sakura-sama.

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:01.570
The word "curse" on Reiji's forehead...

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:05.910
It's written wrong, 
but it's still a demon's curse.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:09.000
It's what's twisting Reiji's mind.

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:12.330
You're being annoying.

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:15.500
Devil Cash Card Cut!

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:19.810
Rokumon-chan!

00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:25.470
Get in my way, and whoever you 
may be, I will show no mercy.

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:30.390
Wait, Reiji!

00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:33.170
Mamiya Sakura!

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:42.010
What are you doing while I'm gone?

00:19:42.010 --> 00:19:43.270
Rokudou-kun.

00:19:44.010 --> 00:19:47.430
Masato is especially ruthless 
towards women and children.

00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:48.750
He's horrifying.

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:50.910
I just realized.

00:19:51.730 --> 00:19:56.380
Rinne-kun, you were nowhere to be 
seen, so I thought you'd run off.

00:19:56.710 --> 00:19:58.070
I was shopping.

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:02.340
Oil Absorbing Sheets!

00:20:05.030 --> 00:20:06.400
<i>Oil Absorbing Sheets.</i>

00:20:06.400 --> 00:20:13.600
<i>A handy item for removing everything from 
curses and spells to dropped food stains.</i>

00:20:16.970 --> 00:20:18.820
The demon curse is gone.

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:22.490
Reiji's twisted mind should 
go back to normal now.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:25.660
What am I...

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:27.670
Nice try, Rinne-kun.

00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:30.640
Reiji may have snapped out of it,

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:33.930
but he can't take back the many 
terrible things he's said and done

00:20:33.930 --> 00:20:36.050
to his friend and girlfriend.

00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:39.670
His broken human relationships 
can't be repaired.

00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:44.630
Right, those two hate me now.

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:46.430
Reiji-san.

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:52.520
Tell Suzu... If she ever finds 
the thing, to throw it out.

00:20:55.310 --> 00:20:57.560
Looks like you have nothing holding 
you to this world anymore.

00:21:02.130 --> 00:21:03.070
Reiji-san!

00:21:03.510 --> 00:21:06.360
Rokumon, take Mamiya Sakura down.

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:08.280
Yes, Rinne-sama.

00:21:08.630 --> 00:21:09.950
Rokudou-kun!

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:11.880
Bye, Rinne-kun.

00:21:12.350 --> 00:21:16.300
As promised, I'm taking Reiji's 
soul back with me to Hell.

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:17.170
Stop!

00:21:19.180 --> 00:21:20.210
What?

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:22.260
Reiji's living spirit...

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:23.920
...just got taken to Hell?

00:21:24.330 --> 00:21:24.970
Yes.

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:27.340
And there's something bothering me.

00:21:27.940 --> 00:21:32.970
Tell Suzu... If she ever finds 
the thing, to throw it out.

00:21:33.470 --> 00:21:34.860
He said that?

00:21:34.860 --> 00:21:37.300
Does it ring a bell?

00:21:37.300 --> 00:21:38.560
I don't know.

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:42.540
But the day he got in a 
crash was my birthday.

00:21:42.540 --> 00:21:43.820
Your birthday?

00:21:44.290 --> 00:21:48.610
Which means maybe he was 
trying to give you something.

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:52.140
<i>Come to think of it, when I first saw him,</i>

00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:54.910
<i>it looked like Reiji-san was 
deep in thought over something.</i>

00:21:55.620 --> 00:21:59.170
<i>He might have lost that </i>thing<i> there.</i>

00:21:59.870 --> 00:22:02.120
<i>For him to become a living 
spirit just to find it,</i>

00:22:02.120 --> 00:22:04.920
<i>it must have been something really precious.</i>

00:22:05.720 --> 00:22:07.760
<i>I have to tell Rokudou-kun.</i>

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:11.580
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:22:12.180 --> 00:22:17.690
<i>Without anything holding him to this world, 
it'll be hard to bring him back to his body.</i>

00:22:20.490 --> 00:22:22.070
<i>Follow me, Rinne-kun.</i>

00:22:22.530 --> 00:22:25.010
<i>I'm going to get even for what you did.</i>

00:22:25.460 --> 00:22:26.570
<i>Come to my home.</i>

00:22:27.990 --> 00:22:29.510
<i>My home... in Hell.</i>

00:24:01.040 --> 00:24:25.980
Next Episode
 Welcome to Hell!

00:24:01.750 --> 00:24:03.720
There are different levels of Hell.

00:24:03.720 --> 00:24:05.000
The Eight Hot Hells,

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:07.090
the Eight Cold Hells, Fox Hell.

00:24:07.090 --> 00:24:09.170
Wow, I never knew there were so many.

00:24:09.170 --> 00:24:13.430
Blood Pool Hell, Needle Hell, Tongue 
Cutting Hell, Poisonous Snake Hell.

00:24:13.820 --> 00:24:15.930
I know one, too, Throat Thrust Hell.

00:24:16.150 --> 00:24:17.930
That's a pro wrestling move.

00:24:17.930 --> 00:24:21.180
Next time on <i>Rin-ne</i>: 
"Welcome to Hell!"

00:24:21.180 --> 00:24:23.190
Oh, and helldivers.

00:24:23.190 --> 00:24:24.500
That's a kind of bird.
